cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use hermeneutic, please cite it as below."
title: "hermeneutic: local correction evidence, retrieval, and deterministic English drift checks"
abstract: >-
  Hermeneutic preserves correction episodes and explicit user/host interpretations
  as scoped, attributed lessons for later agent tasks. Hosts inspect bounded
  candidate context and check applicability before acting. A separate deterministic
  English draft gate checks surface claims. Default lesson retrieval is local
  and lexical; interpretation is explicit. Experimental language mappings remain
  advisory, and broad downstream effectiveness is unmeasured.
type: software
